import Nivat.External.Colle.MinkowskiEdges

/-!
# Zonotopes with the same generator directions have the same edge normals

This file discharges the obligation recorded at `blueprint/NOTE.md:4344-4347`:

> `E(𝒮_{φ_Collé}) = E(𝒮_{φ_KS})` — 二维中边法向只依赖方向、不依赖长度 ⇒
> 方向集相同的两个 zonotope 有相同的边法向集。这是纯凸几何。

## Why it is needed

Collé's Proposition 2.8 is derived from Kari–Szabados Corollary 24, whose `φ_KS` is a
product of *line polynomials*, while Collé's `φ = ∏(X^{hᵢ} − 1)` is a product of
binomials.  The two polynomials are different — `NOTE.md:4331` records that `φ_Collé | ψ`
is **false** — but their Newton polygons are zonotopes generated by segments in the *same
directions*, differing only in the lengths of the generators.  Since `E` only sees
directions, the two polygons have the same edge normals, which is all the downstream
argument uses.

## Contents

The mathematical content is one line: perpendicularity is a property of the direction.
That is already in the tree as `dot_eq_zero_of_det_eq_zero` (`LatticeEdges.lean:1702`).
Everything else is bookkeeping over `E_zono` (`MinkowskiEdges.lean:292`), which reduces
`E` of a Minkowski sum of segments to the union of the `E` of the generators, and
`E_segOf` (`:204`), which says `E (segOf v) = {n | Prim n ∧ dot n v = 0}` — a description
mentioning `v` only through `dot n v = 0`.

## Status

Complete; no `sorry`.  Both theorems measure `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.
-/

namespace Nivat.LE2

open Nivat Pointwise

/-- Two lattice segments in the same direction have the same edge normals. -/
theorem E_segOf_congr {v h : ℤ × ℤ} (hv : v ≠ 0) (hh : h ≠ 0) (hpar : det v h = 0) :
    E (segOf v) = E (segOf h) := by
  have hpar' : det h v = 0 := by simp only [det] at hpar ⊢; linarith
  rw [E_segOf hv, E_segOf hh]
  ext n
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hp, hd⟩
    refine ⟨hp, ?_⟩
    rw [dot_comm]
    exact dot_eq_zero_of_det_eq_zero hv hpar' (by rw [dot_comm]; exact hd)
  · rintro ⟨hp, hd⟩
    refine ⟨hp, ?_⟩
    rw [dot_comm]
    exact dot_eq_zero_of_det_eq_zero hh hpar (by rw [dot_comm]; exact hd)

/-- **Zonotopes with the same generator directions have the same edge normals.**

`𝒮_{φ_Collé}` is generated by the segments `[0, hᵢ]` and `𝒮_{φ_KS}` by `[0, vᵢ]`, with
`⟨vᵢ⟩ = ⟨hᵢ⟩` after reindexing — here `det (v i) (h i) = 0`, the Lean spelling of
`⟨v i⟩ = ⟨h i⟩` for nonzero vectors.  Generator *lengths* are unconstrained, which is
exactly the situation of `NOTE.md:4331` (`φ_KS ≠ φ_Collé` as polynomials, same edge
directions).

Note this is an equality of edge-normal sets, not the weaker "every edge of one is
parallel to some edge of the other" — see `NOTE.md:4352` on why the strong form is the
one to state. -/
theorem E_zono_congr {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι] (s : Finset ι) (v h : ι → ℤ × ℤ)
    (hv : ∀ i ∈ s, v i ≠ 0) (hh : ∀ i ∈ s, h i ≠ 0)
    (hpar : ∀ i ∈ s, det (v i) (h i) = 0) :
    E (∑ i ∈ s, segOf (v i)) = E (∑ i ∈ s, segOf (h i)) := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ i ∈ s, E (segOf (v i)) = E (segOf (h i)) :=
    fun i hi => E_segOf_congr (hv i hi) (hh i hi) (hpar i hi)
  rw [E_zono, E_zono]
  ext n
  simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, exists_prop]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨i, hi, hn⟩
    exact ⟨i, hi, (key i hi) ▸ hn⟩
  · rintro ⟨i, hi, hn⟩
    exact ⟨i, hi, (key i hi).symm ▸ hn⟩

end Nivat.LE2
